                        "review": "[h1]Graze Counter — not for me, and not ready for Steam Deck[/h1]\n\nI only played this for a few minutes, so treat this as a first-impressions review rather than a verdict on the full game. But those few minutes were enough to tell me this isn't for me, and enough to spot problems that have nothing to do with taste.\n\n[h2]Steam Deck: \"Playable\" is doing a lot of work here[/h2]\n\nIt's marked as Playable, and technically that's accurate — it runs, you can play it. But basic things are done badly, and they'd be trivial to fix:\n\n[list]\n[*] [b]B as the default \"continue\" button.[/b] This is backwards from the platform standard and it throws you off constantly.\n[*] [b]Special shot on A[/b], which is an unusual mapping for the genre.\n[*] Various other small defaults that just feel wrong out of the box.\n[/list]\n\nNone of this is a technical limitation. It's a controller layout, and it hasn't been thought through for the Deck.\n\n[b]One genuine positive:[/b] the controls are displayed as a controller diagram before the game starts. That's a good, clear way to do it and I wish more games bothered.\n\n[h2]The intro is confusing[/h2]\n\nStrange and disorienting, and not in a way that made me want to keep going. It doesn't set anything up well.\n\n[h2]Cluttered UI[/h2]\n\nThe in-game UI is hard to read at a glance. Combined with the vertical arcade-style playfield — which I'm personally not a fan of — it makes the whole thing less legible than it needs to be. The vertical format is a genre convention, I get it, but here it actively works against clarity rather than for it.\n\n[h2]The anime girls[/h2]\n\nNot my thing. That's entirely a matter of personal taste and everyone can decide for themselves — but it added to my overall dislike rather than pulling me back in.\n\n[h2]Verdict[/h2]\n\nHonestly? Nothing about it was inviting. I didn't enjoy it, and I stopped early.\n\nTo be fair to the game: [i]a few minutes is not a fair sample[/i], and shmup fans who like vertical arcade layouts and the art style may well get a lot out of it. My complaints about the presentation are subjective. My complaints about the [b]Steam Deck defaults[/b] are not — those are easy fixes that would improve the experience for everyone.\n\n[b]Not recommended, on Deck especially.[/b]",
